From 63c989a883bfbb47c65fa9b796dec29283b62fa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 18:36:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 231/245] feat: Reaper Warden - ipset threat-feed / geo /
 manual-IP firewall (Batch D)

Native feature modeled on Gatekeeper. rc/rwarden.c generates an idempotent apply script (nvram resolved at run time, cold-boot deferral) building a REAPER_WARDEN chain in INPUT+FORWARD: anti-lockout RETURNs (ESTABLISHED,RELATED / LAN subnet / rw_allow) BEFORE any drop; ban/threat/geo sets hit a RW_DROP (optional LOG) sub-chain. Cron updater fetches curated OSS feeds (FireHOL1, Feodo, Spamhaus DROP, DShield) + ipdeny country CIDRs over HTTPS, atomic-swaps rw_threat, caches sets to /jffs. All nvram->shell values charset-validated; feed URLs whitelist-matched. Default OFF. UI Reaper_Warden.asp (reaper-native, in reaper_skip[]) + menu + dash rail + EN.dict RWDN_00-42. IPv4-only + firewall-hook re-arm are follow-ups. Not metal-tested.
